**describeType(value)**

Write `describeType(value)`: return `"null"` for `null`, `"array"` for arrays, and what `typeof` says for everything else.

```js
function describeType(value) {
  // TODO: handle null and arrays before falling back to typeof
  return typeof value;
}
```

back:
// Why: `=== null` is the only reliable null check, and `Array.isArray` the only reliable
// array check. `!value` would also catch 0, "" and undefined; `== null` would also catch
// undefined.
// Docs: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/isArray
function describeType(value) {
  if (value === null) return "null";
  if (Array.isArray(value)) return "array";
  return typeof value;
}

